# @@name@@

A REST API built with [zapline](https://github.com/samsamurai301/zapline): typed
routes, request validation, and OpenAPI docs generated from your code.

```sh
zapline dev          # rebuild and restart on every change
cargo run            # or run once
cargo test           # in-process tests, no sockets
```

Then open:

- <http://localhost:8080/docs>: interactive API docs (Swagger UI)
- <http://localhost:8080/_dev>: the dev console (routes and recent requests; debug builds only)
- <http://localhost:8080/openapi.json>: the OpenAPI 3.1 document
- <http://localhost:8080/health>: liveness probe

```sh
curl -X POST localhost:8080/users \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"name":"Ada","email":"ada@example.com"}'
```

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `src/lib.rs` | `app()`: builds the `App` (OpenAPI docs + routes) |
| `src/main.rs` | Serves `app()`; set `ADDR` to change the bind address (see `.env.example`) |
| `src/models.rs` | Request and response types with validation rules |
| `src/routes/` | One module per resource; each exposes `mount(app)` |
| `tests/` | Integration tests using `app().test()` |

## Adding endpoints

```sh
zapline generate resource post      # src/routes/posts.rs + tests/posts.rs, mounted for you
zapline generate handler ping       # a single route
zapline routes                      # print the route table
zapline openapi -o openapi.json     # export the OpenAPI document
```

## Docker

```sh
docker build -t @@name@@ .
docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 @@name@@
```

The image is a multi-stage build: a Rust toolchain stage compiles the binary and
a slim Debian image runs it as a non-root user.

## CI

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`
and `cargo test` on every push and pull request.
